From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spice-mac <spice-mac@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:52:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] display: add a VideoToolbox decoder for H.264 streams on
 macOS

Decode H.264 video streams with VideoToolbox (hardware, no GStreamer needed):
frames are decoded synchronously as they arrive and the BGRA pictures wait for
their multimedia time, like the builtin MJPEG decoder. Late pictures are only
dropped at display time, since later frames reference them. H.265 is wired up
but opt-in (SPICE_VIDEOTOOLBOX_HEVC=1) until exercised against a server.

Advertise the codecs VideoToolbox decodes, and log the codec and size of each
new stream. SPICE_PREFERRED_VIDEO_CODECS (e.g. "h264,mjpeg") asks the server to
prefer them; it is opt-in because spice-server 0.15.2 can crash when a
GStreamer-encoded stream is torn down.
